  chemistryPair('arrhenius','application','hard',['In a graph of ln k against 1/T, the Arrhenius equation predicts a slope of:','−E_a/R',['+E_a/R','−R/E_a','ln A'],['Write ln k = ln A − E_a/(RT).','Comparing with y = c + mx, the slope with respect to 1/T is −E_a/R.']],['Two pathways have the same pre-exponential factor and temperature. Which has the larger rate constant?','The pathway with lower activation energy',['The pathway with higher activation energy','Both must have identical rate constants','Neither can react'],['The Arrhenius equation gives k = A exp(−E_a/RT).','At the same A and T, reducing E_a makes the exponential factor larger.']])
